EDPEditLast.rexx

For use with the EDPLastBanners.rexx program. Install anywhere you would like,
then add this command, available everywhere:

If you don't install this, then no one can write anything!

  Add this item to your the end of BBSMenu # 2 'Available Everywhere'.

   ELAST   | {#0Pfiles:rexx/EDPEditLast.rexx}
             |         |
            /          \
 control Q of course.    Your path to the program.

OPTIONS:

*************************************************
Banner='You just missed me!'     /* Default Last Banner  */

The default Banner to display, until a user edits it.
Remember that ONLY 40 characters will FIT, so do NOT make it
longer than this.
*************************************************

bans.1="You Just missed me!" /*You may change this default list. */
bans.2="I'm outta here"
bans.3="Well, byebye then!"
bans.4="Time to go already, okay bye everybody."
bans.5="A day for firm decisions.     Or is it?"
bans.6="Easy as 3.1415926789394033"
bans.7="They're coming to take me away....ha ha!"
bans.8="I think to myself what a wonderful WORLD"
bans.9="Don't you people have HOMES?"
bans.10="We ARE the company you keep."

******************************************

As of Vers 2.0, users may have a list of banners, and choose from them.
These variables are what defines the defaults that they will see. Then,
of course, they can edit and change them. Please make sure you keep these
inside the quotes!

Simple to use, really. The program will show you your current last banners 
list, and your current LastBanner, then gives you the option to edit, or
pick from the list. If you don't want to, it cleanly exits.

The menu gives the user the option to edit an item on the list. (And if they
edit one, the program will assume that is the one they want to use.

Or they can choose from the list, which one will be their actual banner!

Or they can have the system choose one for them!

I decided to use this method, because there were some problems and
confusions in using the CNet editors. This is much more precise, anyway.

For the sysop, I added an option to examine any users list, and banner.
I did not write an option to edit a users' list, but if there are requests
for that, I can add it easily.

Enjoy!


